*   **B. Males and females are equally affected with similar disease progression:** In X-linked Alport syndrome (the most common form, suggested by the family history), males are typically more severely affected than females, with earlier onset and faster progression of kidney disease. Females are often carriers and may have variable symptoms",<answer>Option A</answer>,A,A
