    *   **Cervical Spine (C2-C7):** These segments are typical vertebrae with facet joints.
    *   **Facet Joint Orientation:** The facet joints in the cervical spine are oriented primarily in the sagittal plane (more horizontal than lumbar facets).
    *   **Motion Coupling:** Due to the sagittal orientation of the facets, sidebending (lateral flexion) and rotation are coupled movements.
    *   **Direction of Coupling:** When the cervical spine sidebends to the right, it also rotates to the right. When it sidebends to the left, it rotates to the left. Therefore, sidebending and rotation occur in the *same* direction.
