The patient is a 42-year-old woman presenting with an 8-week history of intermittent nausea and abdominal pain. The pain is postprandial (occurs 20-30 minutes after eating), located in the epigastrium radiating to the right upper quadrant (RUQ) and right scapula, lasts about 30 minutes, and is not relieved by antacids. The last episode was triggered by a fatty meal (hamburger and french fries).

