2.  **Identify the likely signaling pathway:** Decreased heart rate and contractility are often associated with increased parasympathetic (vagal) tone or decreased sympathetic tone. The primary neurotransmitter involved in parasympathetic control of the heart is acetylcholine (ACh). ACh acts on muscarinic receptors (specifically M2 receptors) in the heart.

